    {
      "id": "bio1",
      "level": 0,
      "texts": [
        "Ruby Dash was injured last year, and only came back to racing last month.",
        "Green Melody is a new face this year, with only a handful of starts.",
        "Sunny Steps is a seasoned veteran with a wealth of experience.",
        "Violet Dream is a little shy, and not a big fan of the cameras.",
        "Orange Pop was named in a vote by the local kids.",
        "Berry Heart is the crowd favourite, and always gets a big cheer.",
        "Blue Blaze has just moved here from out of town, and everyone is still getting to know this one.",
        "Midnight Star took six months off, and has only just come back to the track.",
        "Mint Breeze comes from a farm up north, and moves especially lightly.",
        "Cocoa Thunder has a chocolate coat, and is the greediest eater in the stable.",
        "Silver Moon only stepped up to the big races this season, and the trainer has high hopes.",
        "Rose Crown comes from a famous family, and walks with real presence."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bio2",
      "level": 0,
      "texts": [
        "Ruby Dash's mother won the Sunny Cup in her day.",
        "Green Melody's trainer says this pony loves soft turf after the rain.",
        "Word is Sunny Steps did an extra lap this morning, and is full of beans.",
        "Violet Dream switched to a new trainer last month.",
        "Orange Pop has had a big appetite lately, and put on a little weight.",
        "Berry Heart came within a whisker of pony of the year last season.",
        "Before every race, Blue Blaze has to walk a lap of the track to settle.",
        "Midnight Star and Orange Pop came from the same stable, so they are old friends.",
        "Mint Breeze has new shoes today, and everyone wants to see the difference.",
        "Cocoa Thunder adores the trainer, and needs a pat on the head before every race.",
        "Silver Moon is named after the white crescent on the forehead.",
        "Before every race, Rose Crown gives a little nod to the stands."
      ]
    },
